I transcribed an identify spell (something
I *think* is going to be _very_ useful) and when I try to cast it is says
'You're too weak to cast this spell."  What does this mean, and how can I
get 'stronger?'  It also says 'The air around you crackles as you goof up.'
Do spells have minimum levels which you must be to use them?  What does
the number in parens after the spell letter mean (i.e. "a) (2) identify")

I prayed, the gods were pleased, my +1 long sword glowed blue.  Now it's
'blessed,' but its it did not go to +2.  What does being blessed mean?  How
will it help?

I 'was momentarily blinded by a flash of light.'  Then the map of the entire
level appeared.  Why?  I know eating a floating eye gives you telepathy
when blind, but I thought it only showed you where the monsters are.

Could someone describe the following: aklys, bardiche, bec de corbin bill-
guisarme, fauchard, glaive, guisarme, halberd, katana, ransuer, spetum, and
voulge?  I looked every one of these up in my dictionary and found not a
one.  It's hard to know what to do with a weapon if you don't know what it
looks like.

If you pray to soon and 'the gods seem angry but nothing seems to happen'
can you ever wait long enough to get blessings/HP again, or must you raise
your luck before the gods will help you?  Is throwing gems at a unicorn the
only way to raise luck?  Seems unfair since unicorns are scarce and it's
hard to throw gems to them.  How do you sacrifice?

What good are fountains?  Of all the times I've dipped something in maybe
once I got an Excalibur.  Most of the time it's "You attract a water nymph"
or "Your weapon rusts!"  Is there any way to tell a good fountain from a
bad?  Is it luck-related?  I generally ignore fountains completely.  Am I
missing something?  If not, may I suggest either making them more useful
in 3.0 or ditching them.  BTW, I have not come across sinks.  Can I have
fountains and no sinks, or are they only on lower levels?

I've been having lots of trouble getting below about 10th level.  I get killed
in some of the most bizarre ways, no matter how careful I am.  What should I
do?  Should I hang out on the lower levels longer to gain experience?  I 
generally move on after finding what I think are all of the rooms/items and
killing most of the monsters.

Any helps/tips/suggestions/etc. would be appreciated.

